

# Proposed Labels and Descriptions for Division F LLC 5 and LLC 6

## LLC 5: Decentralized ISBN Annotation & Collaborative Learning Repository
**Description**: A decentralized platform enabling users to annotate ISBN-linked textbooks and share notes globally, integrated as a widget into LMS platforms (Canvas, Cengage, Moodle, Brightspace). Built on a blockchain-based registry (synergizing with Division F LLC 0), it ensures secure, verifiable annotations while allowing students to access peer insights without stigma. The system uses AI-driven semantic analysis to curate annotations, reducing peer judgment risks by anonymizing contributions (aligned with Division A LLC 2’s consent-based networking). It feeds into Division G LLC 1/2 (credential platforms) by tracking annotation contributions as micro-credentials for corporate recruiters.

**Mechanics**:
- **Annotation Layer**: Users annotate ISBNs via a widget; annotations are stored on a decentralized ledger (IPFS/blockchain, akin to Division F LLC 0).
- **Integration**: API embeds into LMS platforms; supports OAuth2 for secure student email login.
- **Anti-Stigma Design**: Anonymized user IDs prevent peer backlash (e.g., “grossed out” reactions to the marginalized student), with consent toggles inspired by Division A LLC 2.
- **Feedback Loop**: Annotations are rated for quality; high-value contributions signal talent to Division G LLC 7 (employee mobility) and LLC 8 (candidate assessor).

